     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I upon running the model for sampling we get a runtime error, with the message I showed before:</div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-size:14px;line-height:inherit;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(0,0,0);border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;vertical-align:baseline\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:steelblue\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:darkred\">RuntimeError</span>: int variable contained non-int values; processing stage=data initialization; variable name=gap_lengths; base type=int</span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>Changing gap_lengths to an array of reals removes this message.  </div><div><br></div><div>In either case I&#39;m sending an empty list from Python. If I send an empty array, with type &#39;int&#39;, then we don&#39;t get this error. So it does seem to be in the plumbing from Python to Stan.</div></div>"
